{"id":131793,"accession_number":"1954.369","share_license_status":"CC0","tombstone":"Palace Ladies (漢宮春曉圖), 1644–1911. Copy after Qiu Ying (Chinese, 1494–1552). Handscroll; ink and color on silk; overall: 36.2 x 454.4 cm (14 1/4 x 178 7/8 in.). The Cleveland Museum of Art, Gift of I. Theodore Kahn, 1954.369","current_location":null,"title":"Palace Ladies","title_in_original_language":"漢宮春曉圖","creation_date":"1644–1911","creation_date_earliest":1644,"creation_date_latest":1911,"artists_tags":["male"],"culture":["China, Qing dynasty (1644–1911)"],"technique":"handscroll; ink and color on silk","support_materials":[],"department":"Chinese Art","collection":"ASIAN - Handscroll","type":"Painting","measurements":"Overall: 36.2 x 454.4 cm (14 1/4 x 178 7/8 in.)","dimensions":{"overall":{"height":0.362,"height_inch":14,"height_inch_fraction":0.25,"width":4.544,"width_inch":178,"width_inch_fraction":0.875}},"state_of_the_work":null,"edition_of_the_work":null,"copyright":null,"inscriptions":[{"inscription":"漢宮春曉圖.\n劉士瀛","inscription_translation":"Title on frontispiece: Spring Morning in the Han Palace.\nSigned by the calligrapher Liu Shiying, with 2 red seals","inscription_remark":null,"sortorder":1}],"exhibitions":{"current":[{"id":336424,"title":"Facing the Ancestors: Chinese Portraits and Figure Painting – Chinese Gallery Rotation 240a, 241c","description":"<i>Facing the Ancestors: Chinese Portraits and Figure Painting – Chinese Gallery Rotation 240a, 241c</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art (organizer) (August 12, 2019-February 2, 2020).","opening_date":"2019-08-12T04:00:00"}],"legacy":[]},"provenance":[{"description":"I. Theodore Kahn, Cleveland, OH, given to the Cleveland Museum of Art","citations":[],"footnotes":[],"date":"?–1954","sortorder":1},{"description":"The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH","citations":[],"footnotes":[],"date":"1954–","sortorder":2}],"find_spot":null,"related_works":[],"former_accession_numbers":[],"did_you_know":null,"early_education_description":null,"artlens_description":null,"description":"This handscroll illustrates the pursuits of court ladies in a palace precinct on a spring day. Women, young girls, and their maids amuse themselves by sitting on a swing, playing games, watering and admiring peonies, performing music together, playing the <em>qin </em>(zither), feeding a parrot on the balustrade and fish in the water, or catching butterflies. The life of elite women was mostly restricted to the so-called inner quarters, meaning the garden and inner courts of the house. This painting idealizes the world of young palace girls that in fact was often filled with boredom and waiting for a lover.","external_resources":{"wikidata":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60516474"],"internet_archive":["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1954.369-palace-ladies"]},"citations":[{"citation":"Wangwright, Amanda S. \"The Sick Man of Asia.\" In <em>Visualizing the Body in Art, Anatomy, and Medicine Since 1800: Models and Modeling.</em> Andrew Graciano, and Rebecca Marie Messbarger, eds., 180–200. London; New York: Routledge, 2019.","page_number":"Mentioned: p. 187; Reproduced: pl. 8.2","url":null}],"url":"https://clevelandart.org/art/1954.369","images":{"annotation":null,"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1954.369/1954.369_web.jpg","width":"1263","height":"334","filesize":"261037","filename":"1954.369_web.jpg"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1954.369/1954.369_print.jpg","width":"3400","height":"899","filesize":"2564766","filename":"1954.369_print.jpg"},"full":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1954.369/1954.369_full.tif","width":"83933","height":"4868","filesize":"1225811964","filename":"1954.369_full.tif"}},"alternate_images":[{"web":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1954.369/1954.369_alt0_web.jpg","width":"691","height":"893","filesize":"567936"},"print":{"url":"https://openaccess-cdn.clevelandart.org/1954.369/1954.369_alt0_print.jpg","widt